## Step 2 — Adaptive Professional Pledge

To my future self,

I am committing to becoming someone who does not stop learning just because a class or degree is finished. As I move toward a career in nuclear engineering, I want to keep improving my technical knowledge, communication skills, and ability to adapt when things do not go exactly as planned. I know that my career will not develop automatically, so I need to take responsibility for creating opportunities for myself.

I will make an effort to build real professional relationships instead of waiting until I need something from someone. I will talk to professors, attend career events, connect with people in the engineering field, and stay in contact with the people who help me along the way. I will also make sure that my LinkedIn, Handshake, resume, and other professional materials accurately show what I am learning and accomplishing.

I also commit to regularly evaluating my decisions. If a class, internship, or career experience shows me that my current plan needs to change, I will not see that as failure. I will use what I learned to make a better decision.

My goal is not to follow one perfect plan. My goal is to keep learning, building relationships, improving my skills, and making thoughtful adjustments so that I continue moving toward a career that is meaningful to me.
